# Every holder share on a layer, totalled, with what would suspend the total. One row per layer
# naming at least one holder: how many, how many left the share unstated, the sum of the stated
# ones at each of the three points, and the distinct units they were quoted in.
#
# One total for every caller
#   arithmetic/shares_sum.sqlc, arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc and checks/shares_do_not_sum.sqlc
#   each need entries/holders.sqlc grouped by (filing, layer) for the same two numbers. The two
#   arithmetic sites report an unstated share as `suspended` and a foreign unit as
#   `not comparable`. A check working out its own copy, with only a `HAVING` for the first and
#   nothing for the second, would add across units, compare the total with the magnitude, and so
#   disagree with them about the same document.
#
# A share in another unit is not a share of this
#   The shares divide the size of the remainder between the holders, so a share in another unit is
#   not a smaller share; it is not a share of this remainder at all. That is why `share_units` is
#   carried rather than assumed away: a caller compares it with its own layer's unit and decides.
#   arithmetic/roster.sqlc records no unit rule at the `shares_sum` site, which leaves the check
#   the only thing between that site and a wrong number.
#
# Read `unstated` before the sum
#   `sum()` skips NULLs silently, so a layer where half the holders stated a share sums to half the
#   truth and looks like an ordinary number. `unstated` is the column that makes that visible, and
#   every caller reads it before it reads the sum.
#
# A derived share is unstated, and says which identity it waits on
#   `derived` counts the shares filed as `sharesSum`'s output, which are among the unstated ones.
#   Nothing here works out a share, so a caller suspends on them as on any unstated share, and
#   names the identity rather than reading an output as a blank.
-- entries/holders.sqlc folded to one row per layer.
SELECT h.filing, h.layer,
       count(*)                                     AS holders,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE h.share_mode IS NULL)  AS unstated,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE h.share_derivation IS NOT NULL) AS derived,
       sum(h.share_low)                              AS shares_low,
       sum(h.share_mode)                             AS shares_mode,
       sum(h.share_high)                             AS shares_high,
       array_agg(DISTINCT h.share_unit)              AS share_units
FROM (
    :compose(entries/holders.sqlc)
) h
GROUP BY h.filing, h.layer
